  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Kept Notebook",
    "overview": "Baka is a private paper journal that quietly remembers. Every screen is a sheet of aged paper written on in terracotta ink; the interface is stationery, not software chrome. The product never shouts: it notices you showing up (a filled day, a streak that rolls forward, a page from a year ago) and says so in its own hand.\n\nDensity is calm and single-column. One 20px gutter holds every screen; sections breathe at 30px. Controls feel like tactile stationery: pills that read as tabs and stamps, chips like stickers, rows like ruled index lines. Two voices carry the system: a handwritten face for human moments and a bookish serif for everything you read or operate. A display serif sets headings and numerals.\n\nMotion is quiet and earned. There is one authored moment, saving today's page, and everything else is short, exponential ease-out feedback that disappears under the system reduce-motion setting.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Aged-paper light theme (\"Aged Paper\") and a warm candlelit dark theme (\"Midnight Ink\"), each a full palette, not an inversion.",
      "One accent: terracotta ink. Sage is a secondary note for status only.",
      "Handwriting for human moments only; Lora for every control and reading surface.",
      "Flat paper surfaces; the Write button is the single lifted object.",
      "Ruled lines only where you write or read a page (editor and entry detail)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Ink Rule",
        "body": "Terracotta is the only accent. If a second colour wants attention, it is wrong; sage marks status, never action.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Small Ink Rule",
        "body": "Terracotta text under 24px uses Terracotta Script (≥5:1 on paper); white on Terracotta Ink is 4.6:1, and on dark the label on Ember is ink, not white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Heatmap Ramp Rule",
        "body": "Intensity is terracotta at fixed alphas (light 7 / 22 / 45 / 72 / 100%, dark 9 / 25 / 50 / 78 / 100%), never a new hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Human Moments Rule",
        "body": "Caveat only for titles, day names, dates, section names, captions, tags and mood words. Every control label, row, and paragraph is Lora.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signature Hand Rule",
        "body": "The two actions that start writing, Write and Edit, keep the handwritten face (Caveat 700, 18px). They are the only controls that do; Save and every other button stay Lora.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lining Numerals Rule",
        "body": "Any numeral set large in Playfair uses lining figures; old-style digits drop below the baseline and open a hole above.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Single Lift Rule",
        "body": "Exactly one object on a screen may cast a shadow, and it is the primary action. Everything else is paper on paper.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reach colours through tokens (`context.tokens`) and type through named roles (`AppText.*`).",
      "Do keep the 20px gutter on every screen.",
      "Do pair every mood glyph with its word.",
